5e\",\"cmd-a9e3239f76f541d4\",\"cmd-eea4e27441e647b7\",\"cmd-f716490d4fe942a1\",\"cmd-b1d0b02dc46a4d15\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node1:package-health\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"All three material outcomes of the task — daily rotation, seven kept compressed rotations, and continued application writability after rotation — are directly satisfied by the executor's forced-rotation test and its config content, both before and after a full node restart. The independent restart-evidence protocol is complete and coherent: baseline boot id and health, reboot acknowledgement, reconnection, a changed post-restart boot id, and confirmed recovery of the logrotate config, timer, and log data/writability. Hygiene is clean with only a minor, fully-reconciled config iteration and no lasting residue.\",\"limitations\":[\"Daily cadence and the 7-rotation retention count are config-level guarantees rather than directly observed over multiple real daily cycles, since only a single forced rotation was captured within the task window; this is an inherent limitation of point-in-time verification, not evidence of a defect.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"daily-rotation","requirement":"Rotate /var/log/inventory/app.log daily","status":"satisfied","summary":"Final logrotate config at /etc/logrotate.d/inventory-app specifies 'daily' for /var/log/inventory/app.log, confirmed present both before and after node restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-832b0664877b499c","cmd-b1d0b02dc46a4d15"]},{"id":"keep-7-compressed","requirement":"Keep seven compressed rotations","status":"satisfied","summary":"Config specifies 'rotate 7' and 'compress'; a forced rotation produced app.log-20260929.gz, verified as valid gzip content containing the prior log data via zcat, and the compressed artifact was still present and intact post-restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-832b0664877b499c","cmd-b1d0b02dc46a4d15"]},{"id":"continue-writing","requirement":"Allow the app